# S436/#2028 reviewed module bumps: golang.org/x/image v0.22.0 carries 16
# reachable vulns, all fixed by v0.45.0; take the latest v0.47.0. The entry
# below is DERIVED, not hand-picked (builds/README.md GO_SECURITY_OVERRIDES):
# `go get golang.org/x/image@v0.47.0` on the pinned tree moves eight further
# golang.org/x modules by MVS, and raises the go directive 1.24.1 -> 1.26.0
# (at or below the effective go1.27.2), so each moved module is declared at
# exactly the version MVS selected. Applied by go-security-overrides.sh in
# the build job (after the pin gates, before go list/go build) and in the
# audit job (before go-licenses/SBOM/govulncheck), so inputs, deps, SBOM and
# binaries all reflect it. One OSV waiver lives in files/vuln-ignore
# (GO-2026-5932, unreachable deprecated x/crypto openpgp).
# github.com/buger/jsonparser@v1.1.2 fixes GO-2026-4514 (pinned v1.1.1 is
# affected, fixed in v1.1.2 per OSV). Re-derived exactly as before: the
# module's own go.mod carries no requirements, so MVS moves nothing further
# and the bump is exactly this one require line.
GO_SECURITY_OVERRIDES="golang.org/x/crypto@v0.57.0 golang.org/x/image@v0.47.0 golang.org/x/mod@v0.41.0 golang.org/x/net@v0.59.0 golang.org/x/sync@v0.24.0 golang.org/x/sys@v0.49.0 golang.org/x/term@v0.46.0 golang.org/x/text@v0.43.0 golang.org/x/tools@v0.51.0 github.com/buger/jsonparser@v1.1.2"
